      "contextFingerprint": "815af0332eb1fc9481d782a6eb1dbf6e018804436213c7aa53e684981820d439",
      "sourceText": "| 示例 | 讲了什么 | 新出现的语法 | 为什么这样写 | 注意事项 |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| 示例 1 | 基础类型别名 | `using Name = Type;` | 语法更直观，`=` 让人一眼看出\"别名 = 原类型\" | typedef 也能做，但 using 更清晰 |\n| 示例 2 | 函数指针别名 | `using Func = int(*)(int,int);` | 名字在中间，比 typedef 的名字夹在中间更好读 | 实际项目中建议用 `std::function` 代替裸函数指针 |\n| 示例 3 | 模板别名 | `template<T> using Vec = vector<T>;` | typedef 做不到模板别名，这是 using 的独特能力 | 非常适合简化嵌套模板类型 |\n| 示例 4 | using 不是新类型 | `using Meter = double`、包装结构体 | 别名提升可读性，结构体提供类型安全 | 需要防止参数传反时，不要只靠 using |",
      "translatedText": "| Example | What was explained | Newly introduced syntax | Why it is written this way | Notes |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| Example 1 | Basic type alias | `using Name = Type;` | The syntax is more intuitive,`=` making it clear at a glance that \"alias = original type\" | typedef can also do this, but using is clearer |\n| Example 2 | Function pointer alias | `using Func = int(*)(int,int);` | The name is in the middle, which is easier to read than typedef where the name is sandwiched in the middle | In actual projects, it is recommended to use `std::function` instead of raw function pointers |\n| Example 3 | Template alias | `template<T> using Vec = vector<T>;` | typedef cannot do template aliases; this is a unique capability of using | Very suitable for simplifying nested template types |\n| Example 4 | using is not a new type | `using Meter = double`、wrapper struct | Aliases improve readability, structs provide type safety | When it is necessary to prevent arguments from being passed in the wrong order, do not rely only on using |",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 277,
        "outputTokens": 192,
        "costUsd": 0.000314
      }
    },
